{
  "about": "Performance budget of the storefront audit (setup/audit/lighthouse.mjs). Each page fails the lighthouse workflow when the median of its runs is worse than its reference value moved by the tolerance of the metric and preset: lower for a score, higher for a time, a shift, a weight or a request count. The reference is a measure of the workflow itself, written here by hand with its date and commit: it is raised when an improvement is acquired, never rewritten from the last run.",
  "toleranceBasis": "2026-11-17, two measures of the same code (core 155cbe071 and af9ed4f3b, which differ only in the labels of the workflow, Flexy dev-main bf04b3b4d) on GitHub runners. Desktop medians moved by 2 points of performance and 19 % of FCP and LCP at most. Mobile, simulated by Lighthouse on a slow 4G, moved by steps: up to 15 points of performance and 72 % of LCP, so its times only catch a gross regression. Accessibility, best practices, SEO, CLS, TBT, weight (under 0.2 %) and requests did not move on either preset: they hold the tight thresholds.",
